    "turns": [
     {
      "rc": 0,
      "timed_out": false,
      "stopped": null,
      "wall_s": 11.943657270865515,
      "peak_mb": 80.578125,
      "stdout_tail": "I'll start by looking at the repo structure and running the tests.\nThe bug was in `stats.py:8`: `mean` divided the sum by `len(values) - 1` (a variance-style denominator) instead of `len(values)`. That gave `3.333...` for `[1, 2, 3, 4]` and crashed with `ZeroDivisionError` for a single-element list.\n\nChanged it to divide by `len(values)`. All 3 tests pass now (`python3 -m unittest -v` \u2192 OK).\n",
      "stderr_tail": "construct: made /tmp/construct-bench/task/orca-smoke/home private (755 -> 700); see docs/adr/0021\n\u00b7 shell {\"command\": \"find . -type f -not -path './.git/*' | head -50 && echo \\\"---\\\" && git log --oneline | head -5\"}\n\u00b7 shell {\"command\": \"python3 -m unittest 2>&1 | head -50\"}\n\u00b7 read {\"path\": \"stats.py\"}\n\u00b7 read {\"path\": \"test_stats.py\"}\n\u00b7 read {\"path\": \"README.md\"}\n\u00b7 edit {\"path\": \"stats.py\", \"old_string\": \"    return sum(values) / (len(values) - 1)\", \"new_string\": \"    return sum(values) / len(values)\"}\n\u00b7 shell {\"command\": \"python3 -m unittest -v 2>&1 | tail -15\"}\n"
     },
     {
      "rc": 0,
      "timed_out": false,
      "stopped": null,
      "wall_s": 12.043981848983094,
      "peak_mb": 81.08203125,
      "stdout_tail": "Added `median` to `stats.py`, which sorts a copy of the input, returns the middle element for odd lengths, averages the two middle ones for even lengths, and raises `ValueError` on an empty list. Added a `MedianTest` class in `test_stats.py` covering odd, even, single-element, unsorted, and empty inputs.\n\nVerified with `python3 -m unittest -v`: all 8 tests pass.\n",
      "stderr_tail": "\u00b7 edit {\"path\": \"stats.py\", \"old_string\": \"    return sum(values) / len(values)\", \"new_string\": \"    return sum(values) / len(values)\\n\\n\\ndef median(values):\\n    \\\"\\\u2026\n\u00b7 edit {\"new_string\": \"from stats import mean, median\", \"old_string\": \"from stats import mean\", \"path\": \"test_stats.py\"}\n\u00b7 edit {\"new_string\": \"            mean([])\\n\\n\\nclass MedianTest(unittest.TestCase):\\n    def test_odd(self):\\n        self.assertEqual(median([3, 1, 2]), 2)\\n\\n    d\u2026\n\u00b7 shell {\"command\": \"python3 -m unittest -v 2>&1 | tail -20\"}\n"
     },
     {
      "rc": 0,
      "timed_out": false,
      "stopped": null,
      "wall_s": 7.309822600102052,
      "peak_mb": 79.84765625,
      "stdout_tail": "Documented `mean` and `median` under `## API` in README.md with a short usage example each; all 8 tests still pass.\n\nAcross this session I fixed the `mean` divisor bug (`len(values) - 1` \u2192 `len(values)`), added a `median` function with tests, and documented both functions in the README.\n",
      "stderr_tail": "\u00b7 edit {\"new_string\": \"Small statistics helpers.\\n\\n## API\\n\\n### `mean(values)`\\n\\nArithmetic mean of a non-empty list of numbers; raises `ValueError` on an empty lis\u2026\n\u00b7 shell {\"command\": \"python3 -m unittest 2>&1 | tail -3 && git diff --stat\"}\n"
     }
